From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:47:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] end the recording when the camera closes with a recoverable
 error

When CameraX closes the camera with a recoverable error and opens it
again (the camera device reports ERROR_CAMERA_DEVICE, or an open that
fails is retried), the recording in progress goes on across the gap and
holds whatever the new session delivers, a stall and then dark frames,
until the person stops it. CameraX ends a recording only on an explicit
stop, a use case that is detached, a limit or an encoder error, so no
camera error ends it alone.

End the current recording where the app handles that error, through one
view model function that the shutter uses as well. The recorder
finalizes with no error, the clip ends where the camera did and is
offered as for any other recording, and the app stays open and opens its
camera again by itself. A paused recording ends the same way, and
nothing happens when no video is recording.

A stopped recording is closed, so pause, resume and mute throw on it,
while the screen keeps showing it until it finalizes, about a second
later when no frames come. The function marks the recording as ending,
with its identity, until its own Finalize event has reset the state. In
that time the pause or resume button and the call that mutes the
recording do nothing (the microphone setting still applies to the next
recording), and a second stop does nothing. The button pressed when no
recording runs, as a press queued behind the Finalize is, is logged and
ignored where it used to throw.

The Finalize event retires the handle of its own recording, and before
it publishes idle: the next recording may start as soon as the state is
idle and store its own handle, which a late event must not take. A
recording that finalizes before its handle is stored retires it when it
is stored.

A start that still waits for its sound has no recording to stop: it is
cancelled, the state goes back to idle and the activity puts the shutter
back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../org/lineageos/aperture/CameraActivity.kt  |  11 +-
 .../aperture/viewmodels/CameraViewModel.kt    | 112 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/CameraActivity.kt b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/CameraActivity.kt
index a1f5caa90d4d66ca80f4fa28910d7a3d60e3a95f..38512bdf2875c8d32f91fd51aebf3116b2c95d71 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/CameraActivity.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/CameraActivity.kt
@@ -804,7 +804,16 @@ open class CameraActivity : AppCompatActivity(R.layout.activity_camera) {
                         }
 
                         CameraXCameraState.ERROR_OTHER_RECOVERABLE_ERROR -> {
-                            // Warn the user and don't do anything
+                            // The camera is closed and CameraX opens it again, so a
+                            // recording would go on across the gap: end it and save the
+                            // clip. There is nothing to end when no video is recording
+                            if (viewModel.endVideoRecording()) {
+                                // A start that was still waiting has no recording to
+                                // finalize, put the shutter back here
+                                startShutterAnimation(ShutterAnimation.VideoEnd)
+                            }
+
+                            // Warn the user
                             showToast(R.string.error_other_recoverable_error)
                         }
 
diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/viewmodels/CameraViewModel.kt b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/viewmodels/CameraViewModel.kt
index bc83de246e4288742eb3a6288bd4e66623dbefc4..f0879784670702f0f19af6b4821d0aa62659a5dc 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/viewmodels/CameraViewModel.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/aperture/viewmodels/CameraViewModel.kt
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ import androidx.lifecycle.asFlow
 import androidx.lifecycle.viewModelScope
 import kotlinx.coroutines.Dispatchers
 import kotlinx.coroutines.ExperimentalCoroutinesApi
+import kotlinx.coroutines.Job
 import kotlinx.coroutines.channels.awaitClose
 import kotlinx.coroutines.delay
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.MutableSharedFlow
@@ -96,7 +97,10 @@ import org.lineageos.aperture.utils.StorageUtils
 import java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream
 import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService
 import java.util.concurrent.Executors
+import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicBoolean
 import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger
+import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong
+import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReference
 import kotlin.reflect.safeCast
 
 /**
@@ -808,6 +812,24 @@ class CameraViewModel(application: Application) : ApertureViewModel(application)
      */
     val videoRecording = MutableStateFlow<Recording?>(null)
 
+    /**
+     * The start of a video recording that still waits for its sound, see [captureVideo].
+     */
+    private var videoRecordingStart: Job? = null
+
+    /**
+     * The number of video recordings started, which gives each one its identity.
+     */
+    private val videoRecordingCount = AtomicLong()
+
+    /**
+     * The identity of the video recording that [endVideoRecording] stopped and that has not
+     * finalized yet, or 0. A stopped [Recording] is closed, pause, resume and mute throw on it.
+     * The mark counts only while it is the identity of the recording started last, so it can
+     * never hold back a recording that starts after it.
+     */
+    private val endingVideoRecording = AtomicLong()
+
     val isVideoMicButtonEnabled = combine(
         cameraState,
         videoRecording,
@@ -1169,7 +1191,7 @@ class CameraViewModel(application: Application) : ApertureViewModel(application)
         if (cameraState.value != CameraState.IDLE) {
             if (cameraController.isRecording) {
                 // Stop the current recording session.
-                videoRecording.value?.stop()
+                endVideoRecording()
             }
             return
         }
@@ -1190,11 +1212,18 @@ class CameraViewModel(application: Application) : ApertureViewModel(application)
         // Play shutter sound
         val delayTime = if (cameraSoundsUtils.playStartVideoRecording()) 500L else 0L
 
-        viewModelScope.launch {
+        val recordingId = videoRecordingCount.incrementAndGet()
+
+        videoRecordingStart = viewModelScope.launch {
             delay(delayTime)
 
+            // The handle of this recording, which only its own Finalize event retires, and
+            // whether that event came before the handle was stored
+            val started = AtomicReference<Recording?>()
+            val finalized = AtomicBoolean()
+
             // Start recording
-            videoRecording.value = cameraController.startRecording(
+            val recording = cameraController.startRecording(
                 outputOptions,
                 videoAudioConfig,
                 cameraExecutor,
@@ -1232,20 +1261,87 @@ class CameraViewModel(application: Application) : ApertureViewModel(application)
                                 mediaRepository.broadcastNewVideo(it.outputResults.outputUri)
                             }
                         }
+                        // Retire the handle before the state goes idle: from idle on the
+                        // next recording may start and store its own at once, and the handle
+                        // retired is this recording's only
+                        finalized.set(true)
+                        videoRecording.compareAndSet(started.get(), null)
                         cameraState.value = CameraState.IDLE
-                        videoRecording.value = null
+
+                        // Only now is the recording over for its controls: clear its mark,
+                        // and no later recording's
+                        endingVideoRecording.compareAndSet(recordingId, 0L)
                     }
                 }
             }
+
+            started.set(recording)
+            videoRecording.value = recording
+            if (finalized.get()) {
+                // It finalized before its handle was stored, retire the handle now
+                videoRecording.compareAndSet(recording, null)
+            }
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * End the video recording, for the shutter and for a camera that closes under it.
+     *
+     * A start that still waits for its sound is cancelled and the state goes back to idle: there
+     * is no recording to finalize, so the caller puts the shutter back. A recording that runs or
+     * is paused is stopped and marked as ending until its Finalize event, because a stopped
+     * [Recording] is closed (pause, resume and mute throw on it) while the UI keeps showing it
+     * until it finalizes, a second or so later when no frames come. Stopping it again does
+     * nothing.
+     *
+     * Call it on the main thread.
+     *
+     * @return true when it cancelled a start that was waiting
+     */
+    fun endVideoRecording(): Boolean {
+        if (videoRecordingStart?.isActive == true) {
+            videoRecordingStart?.cancel()
+            cameraState.value = CameraState.IDLE
+            Log.d(LOG_TAG, "The start of the video recording is cancelled")
+            return true
+        }
+
+        val recording = videoRecording.value ?: return false
+        val recordingId = videoRecordingCount.get()
+        if (endingVideoRecording.getAndSet(recordingId) != recordingId) {
+            Log.d(LOG_TAG, "The video recording is stopped")
+            recording.stop()
+        }
+        return false
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Whether the video recording was stopped and has not finalized yet, see [endVideoRecording].
+     *
+     * @param what What the caller was about to do to the recording, for the log
+     */
+    private fun isVideoRecordingEnding(what: String): Boolean {
+        val endingId = endingVideoRecording.get()
+        if (endingId == 0L || endingId != videoRecordingCount.get()) {
+            return false
+        }
+
+        Log.d(LOG_TAG, "$what is ignored, the video recording ends")
+        return true
+    }
+
     fun onVideoRecordingStateButtonPress() {
+        if (isVideoRecordingEnding("The pause or resume")) {
+            return
+        }
+
         when (cameraState.value) {
             CameraState.RECORDING_VIDEO -> videoRecording.value?.pause()
             CameraState.RECORDING_VIDEO_PAUSED -> videoRecording.value?.resume()
-            else -> error(
-                "videoRecordingStateButton clicked while in invalid state: ${cameraState.value}"
+            // A press queued behind the Finalize finds no recording, do not throw
+            else -> Log.w(
+                LOG_TAG,
+                "The pause or resume is ignored, no recording runs (${cameraState.value})",
             )
         }
     }
@@ -1527,7 +1623,9 @@ class CameraViewModel(application: Application) : ApertureViewModel(application)
             false -> AudioConfig.AUDIO_DISABLED
         }
 
-        videoRecording.value?.mute(!videoMicrophoneEnabled)
+        if (!isVideoRecordingEnding("Muting the recording")) {
+            videoRecording.value?.mute(!videoMicrophoneEnabled)
+        }
 
         this.videoMicMode.value = videoMicrophoneEnabled
 
